  "problem": "Hospital JSON MRF samples could treat official fictional CMS examples as live files. An unknown newer schema version could be reported as compatible. A budget stop could be treated as whole-file validation. Numeric, string, percentage, algorithm and per-diem charges could collapse into comparable dollar prices. 2026 allowed-amount percentile/median fields could be relabeled as patient bills. File-level schema validity could be claimed from a partial sample. A full-size MRF download could start without a budget.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Hospital JSON parsing lives in packages/connectors/mrf/hospital-json.mjs. CMS JSON v3.0.0 is pinned from hospital-price-transparency commit 5333564a710f80d7740180b9ffab8dbdcba9b502. Official fictional examples are marked synthetic. Unknown newer versions fail closed. Historical v2 is labeled historical and not compatible. A budget stop yields a partial sample with unknown file-schema validity. Algorithm, percentage and per-diem charges remain non-comparable. Allowed-amount median/percentile fields are preserved as allowed-amount elements. No full-size MRF download is initiated. Sealed identity src is unchanged. Last-good generation live-2026-09-03-85b50522b420 is unchanged.",
